"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIt is said that a video titled Real Estate Mystery - The Strange House released on a personal YouTube channel gained popularity and was released as a book.  \n\nIt is a composition that deduces the strange sense of incongruity hidden in a seemingly ordinary house floor plan in a dialogue format.  \n\nIn a seemingly ordinary house floor plan, there exists a  that is completely isolated without being connected to any door.  \nThis irrational structure felt a sense of incongruity, and the story begins when the narrator seeks advice from an acquaintance who is an architectural designer.  \n\nThe way the story unfolded and the ideas were fresh. But that's about it.  \nIt started well, but it was nothing more than forced motives, processes, and a patched-up ending.  \n\nMaybe because I didn't know the video was the original, it was hard to read towards the end.  \nIt wasn't because the content was difficult, but I was worried if I should continue reading this forcedness.  \n\nShould something like this have been published? Such stories and developments definitely resonate more in videos.\n"